WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.733
Step-by-step installation of REau Lite

2
00:00:03.733 --> 00:00:10.400
1. Download the REau Lite APK from the project's Releases page and open the file to install it

3
00:00:10.400 --> 00:00:16.467
Lite and Full can be installed together, but only one can be on at a time

4
00:00:16.467 --> 00:00:22.467
2. Open REau Lite and scroll the terms of use to the end, or tap Scroll to the end

5
00:00:22.467 --> 00:00:25.467
Then tap I accept

6
00:00:25.467 --> 00:00:31.733
3. Allow location while using the app: it is only used to find the dash's Wi-Fi

7
00:00:31.733 --> 00:00:35.267
Also allow the suggested Wi-Fi networks

8
00:00:35.267 --> 00:00:39.400
4. Tap Turn on and allow notifications

9
00:00:39.400 --> 00:00:46.867
5. On Lite, the Android Auto server is turned on by hand: tap Open Android Auto settings

10
00:00:46.867 --> 00:00:50.267
Scroll to the bottom and tap Version ten times

11
00:00:50.267 --> 00:00:54.600
Confirm: Enable developer settings, OK

12
00:00:54.600 --> 00:00:59.400
In the three-dot menu, tap Start head unit server

13
00:00:59.400 --> 00:01:06.000
The server turns off when the session ends and after restarting the phone: turn it on again every time

14
00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:13.333
6. Go back to REau Lite. The first time, tap Connect so Android lets it join the dash's Wi-Fi

15
00:01:13.333 --> 00:01:18.533
With Android Auto active and the dash ready, REau Lite is streaming

16
00:01:18.533 --> 00:01:23.333
7. In Permissions, tap Ask for the missing ones and allow everything

17
00:01:23.333 --> 00:01:29.667
Exclude REau from battery optimization, so Android does not pause the app with the screen off

18
00:01:29.667 --> 00:01:35.067
Done. Set the route in Waze and put the phone away. To finish, tap Turn off

